     quantity/ADD TO CART/Buy-with-Shop bar, not just the Buy-with-Shop
     column it lives in. CSS alone can't do this: the link sits several
     levels inside .shopify-payment-button (a `position:relative` ancestor
     needed for its own colour-overlay ::before/::after), so an
     absolutely-positioned child of it is confined to ITS width, not the
     whole bar's -- a plain `width:100%` or negative margin can't reach
     past that ancestor boundary. Measuring both rects directly and
     setting left/width in real pixels sidesteps it. The Shop Pay wallet
     button is a lazy-loaded web component, so this can't just run once
     at load -- a MutationObserver on its container catches the link
